  {
   "approach": "The west-side approach starts on the Slesse Creek road, where a very steep climbers' trail climbs straight to treeline. Traverse the meadowed slopes toward the west face of the summit tower, then follow the scrambling route toward the southwest gully across the ledges beneath the face. The pillar starts where you have crossed most of those ledges and are about to enter the gully proper. Road access in that valley has been restricted, so check before relying on it.",
   "area_id": "bc_slesse_mountain",
