  {
   "approach": "Start at the end of the park road at the Bugaboo Creek trailhead and take the Conrad Kain Hut trail, about 5 km one way with roughly 700 m of gain, steep and with chained sections near the top. Climbers camp at the hut or at the Applebee Dome campground on the rock slab above it. The route starts at the far left (south) side of the east face: look for the big pillar shaped like an elephant trunk and start to its right, up a short finger crack from the glacier. descend to the glacier below the wall and walk to the base, stepping across the moat at the rock, which gets harder as summer goes on. Bring an axe and rope for the glacier.",
